1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,460
Your demo works.

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,440
Your colleague still can't use it.

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,200
You own the experience for a partner

4
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:08,940
pilot; peers own access and operations.

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,330
Give your agent the Converge methodology,

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,260
shared agreements, and project access.

7
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:18,500
Have it inspect reality and its tools, expose consequential

8
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,340
gaps, and choose next steps within those agreements.

9
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:26,140
Make the pilot journey ready, including acceptance, refusal, and handoff.

10
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,640
Choose implementation details within our agreements.

11
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,920
Stay within this budget and stop when the outcome is verified.

12
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,860
Access policy and the external launch

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,900
decision remain with their named owners.

14
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:41,900
The agent carries planning, implementation, coordination,

15
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,160
integration, checking, and repair within that authority.

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,220
Use relevant prior results to judge what the workflow can carry.

17
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,920
Where evidence is weak, try a representative complete journey.

18
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,140
Can it operate the interface, follow

19
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,200
the handoff, and detect a broken result?

20
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,660
Give it responsibility supported by that evidence, and adjust as you learn.

21
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,420
Clear instructions help; the tools, context,

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,120
and capabilities have to support them.

23
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,200
Missing capability stays visible instead

24
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,980
of becoming your routine testing job.

25
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:17,100
A reversible layout choice is within scope: try it, check it, adjust.

26
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:18,940
Missing evidence?

27
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,140
Investigate it.

28
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,920
A change to a shared commitment goes to the owner with the

29
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,760
authority to settle it, with options and a recommendation.

30
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,500
Hold only the work that depends on that choice.

31
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:32,780
Being available doesn't make you the approval desk for ordinary decisions.

32
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:36,960
For larger work, agents keep assignments, ownership,

33
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,860
dependencies, and decisions in a durable record.

34
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:44,140
Choose focused parts and repositories where better understanding

35
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:47,260
and independent work justify the coordination they add.

36
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,620
Someone coordinates the combined result.

37
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,760
After an interruption, the next worker checks

38
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,080
what actually happened before continuing.

39
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,060
A missing response is not a reason to repeat

40
00:01:58,060 --> 00:01:59,640
an action that may already be complete.

41
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:04,140
The workflow exercises the experience a partner will receive.

42
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,660
It submits, accepts, refuses, and transfers

43
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,960
a request, then checks the visible owner.

44
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,580
If a component passes but the partner sees

45
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:15,190
the wrong team, the promise is still broken.

46
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:16,560
Repair and recheck.

47
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:20,200
Return the result, the evidence, and the remaining limits.

48
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,640
Release follows the authority already agreed.

49
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,800
You judge whether the experience serves the

50
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,720
need and whether the checks deserve confidence.

51
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:33,100
You may need a colleague's expertise or sustained time with the product.

52
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,100
Give feedback naturally.

53
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:38,880
The agent investigates, carries the correction into the work,

54
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,020
and updates the guidance or check that should prevent a repeat.

55
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:46,260
When the destination changes, reassess from today's reality.

56
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,680
Bring peers an update they can act on: what is now

57
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:52,220
true, what affects their work, and what needs judgment.

58
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,840
Carry your commitment through, keep the agreements

59
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,160
current, and help improve how the team works.

60
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,240
Converge connects our shared direction

61
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,140
with the work each of us can now lead.

62
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,240
That is how greater individual capability

63
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,590
can become greater collective capability.